    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "align": "left",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This video establishes a timeline of the humble origins of fan editing as a form of participatory culture. Early fan edits were primarily in small niche internet spaces that were shared by fans as a way to express their connection to media. The labor going into slicing and mixing the videos functioning as a celebratory act of the media. Understanding this history is important because it allows us to understand how current-day edits are circulated and contribute to an advertising-filled system."
        }
      ]
